// CLAIM: No catch or recover
// HOLDS: refused
// REFUSED-BECAUSE: expected `=`, `+=`, `-=` or `*=`, found `{`
// WHY: a failure exits 70 and there is no handler. A `catch` that parses means a program can
//      swallow a contract violation, which is the opposite of what contracts are for.
region main {
    try {
        print("body");
    } catch (problem) {
        print("caught");
    }
}
